%% Build spectrum — Ways to Build & Deliver Apps.
%% Decision flow: already have an image? -> no image, have source -> S2I or a Containerfile,
%% depending on whether you need control of the base image and build steps -> once the build
%% belongs to the team (every push: test, scan, sign), it moves into a pipeline. Node order and
%% wording follow concept.adoc's "Two build strategies — and where pipelines fit" verbatim.
%% Resized 2026-08-22: graph TD (524x1259, text at 1.72x) -> flowchart LR. A spectrum reads
%% left-to-right, so flipping direction is the fix; also merged two 3-line labels (Q2, Q3) down
%% to 2 lines each by removing a line break, not a word.
flowchart LR
  START([You have an app to run]) --> Q1{Do you already<br/>have an image?}
  Q1 -->|Yes| DEPLOY[Deploy from image<br/>no build]
  Q1 -->|No, I have source| Q2{Do you need control<br/>of the base image and build steps?}
  Q2 -->|No, just build it| S2I[Import from Git<br/>Source-to-Image]
  Q2 -->|Yes| DOCKER[Containerfile build<br/>Buildah]
  S2I --> Q3{Does the build belong<br/>to the team now? · every push, test, scan, sign}
  DOCKER --> Q3
  Q3 -->|Yes| PIPE[Run the same build<br/>from a Pipeline · separate module]
  Q3 -->|Not yet| DONE([Running app])
  DEPLOY --> DONE
  classDef pick fill:#e00,stroke:#900,color:#fff;
  class DEPLOY,S2I,DOCKER pick;
  classDef later fill:#fff,stroke:#900,color:#900,stroke-dasharray: 4 3;
  class PIPE later;
